\begin{center}
{\Large\itshape\color{ChapterBrown} תְּהִלִּים}\\[0.1cm]
{\small\itshape\color{LightGray} Tehillim · 「讚美之歌」——全卷的希伯來名字}

\vspace{0.8cm}

\lyresymbol\hspace{0.2cm}{\color{ScriptureGold}\rule{1.8in}{0.8pt}}\hspace{0.2cm}\lyresymbol

\vspace{0.8cm}

{\large\bfseries\color{ChapterBrown} 關於本書}\qquad{\large\bfseries\color{ChapterBrown} About This Book}

\vspace{0.5cm}

\begin{minipage}{5in}
\small\color{TextGray}
$if(backcover)$
$backcover$
$else$
本書依詩篇本身的五卷結構（對應摩西五經），分五冊研讀全卷一百五十篇：卷一（詩1--41，有福的人）、卷二（詩42--72，拯救與王）、卷三（詩73--89，聖所與約）、卷四（詩90--106，曠野與耶和華作王）、卷五（詩107--150，話語、回歸、頌讚）。全書採用黃長老的查經方法——濃縮精義、以經解經、從耶穌的角度讀每一篇——因為詩篇一百五十篇，主角永遠是耶穌：受苦的（詩22）、牧養的（詩23）、掌權的（詩24）、君王兼祭司的（詩110）、被棄而成為房角石的（詩118）。整卷詩篇的終局，是「凡有氣息的，都要讚美耶和華」（詩150:6）——與整本聖經的終局，同一個方向。

A five-volume study of all 150 psalms following the Psalter's own five-book structure mirroring the Pentateuch. Reading with Elder Huang's method — distilling the essence, interpreting Scripture with Scripture, and reading every psalm from the angle of Jesus Christ: the suffering shepherd (Ps 22), the good shepherd (Ps 23), the King of glory (Ps 24), the priest-king (Ps 110), the rejected cornerstone (Ps 118). The Psalter ends where the whole Bible ends: "Let everything that has breath praise the LORD" (Ps 150:6).
$endif$
